  "result": {
    "summary": "Two identical 2,048-hand cohorts produced bit-identical logical trajectory SHA256 and 5,918 public-opponent decisions each. All actions were legal and replayable, every street plus fold/call/four raise slots were covered, and 256 private-hole perturbations had zero probability error. Standard10 scored +97.7959 bb/100 against the model on the unique cohort.",
    "conclusion": "The frozen public-state opponent is a valid replayable physical-v6 behavior model but is exploitable, so it is suitable only as a minority identity in a diverse league, not as a champion or sole training opponent.",
    "decision": "ADMIT_PUBLIC_OPPONENT_WORKER_INTEGRATION",
    "next_step": "Add a default-off worker path for a bounded public-opponent fraction, with exact accounting and fixed-seed replay; run a short matched Standard10-initialized hero smoke against the same diverse league before scaling."
  },
